From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: report the current QTVR node after navigation

QTVR mouseOver saves the node before dispatching a button-up event.  The
event may navigate to another panorama node, but the legacy return string
still uses the saved pre-click value.  Consumers therefore receive the
previous node and display navigation state one step behind.

Refresh the saved node after event dispatch.  This preserves the existing
node-change and hotspot logic while ensuring both jump return paths report
the node now displayed by the decoder.
---
 engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp b/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp
--- a/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp
@@ -252,6 +252,7 @@ void QTVR::m_mouseOver(int nargs) {
 
 				if (me->_video->getCurrentNodeID() != node)
 					nodeChanged = true;
+				node = me->_video->getCurrentNodeID();
 
 				hotspot = me->_video->getClickedHotspotID();
 
